text.oreville.jsijsj=Morphs	#
text.oreville.idhbws=§7§oNote: Morphs currently do not show in Multiplayer, only you will see the Morph you have selected. They are also Expressions compatible, so we hope all of our console friends can now enjoy a slice of the Expressions feature!	#
text.oreville.fnfxwa=3D Tools: §7At long last, you can now play with 3D tools!	#
text.oreville.vcsxkk=Replace traditional 2D tools with fully custom 3D models.	#
text.oreville.ofirha=Sword, Trident, Axe, Pickaxe, Shovel, Hoe.	#
text.oreville.frvfho=Updated the 2D planes on the trident to be slightly 3D.	#
text.oreville.znaare=Costumes: §7Turns some leather armour with trims into custom themed costumes. Only works with the Full Experience texture style.	#
text.oreville.sbjrwy=Item Swap Sounds: §7Play a sound whenever you switch items in your hotbar.	#
text.oreville.nersjw=Better Rain Particles: §7Choose between custom rain particles or the vanilla rain look. We are unable to change the colour of the rain from Blue to Grey in Vanilla & Custom Experience as this particle is hard coded. This feature just includes the raindrop particles.	#
text.oreville.cbgaoc=Legacy Baby Chick Design: §7Switch between the new Tiny Takeover Chick and Legacy Actions & Stuff Chick model. You can also use the nametag "Peep" or "Hatchling" to have a mixture of both designs!	#
text.oreville.rjraqd=Axolotl Colour: §7Pick the colour of your axolotl in a bucket when you hold it in hand. Choose between Pink, Gold, Cyan, Brown, and Blue.	#
text.oreville.mosrst=Morphs: §7Replace your default player model with a range of fully custom 3D characters, each with different visuals, effects, and unique animations. Read the Morphs section for more information.	#
text.oreville.ptssyx=Entity Biome Variants: §7Choose if special biome mob variants can spawn on their own, or only appear when you name a mob with a nametag.	#
text.oreville.xrudoc=Armour Visibility: §7Choose how equipped armour shows up on you. See it on your arms in first person, keep the normal vanilla look, or hide it completely.	#
text.oreville.gmhjvp=Tool Enchantment Glint: §7Choose how enchanted tools look in your hand. Add a custom outline, a custom glint, enable both, or turn both off and keep the vanilla style.	#
text.oreville.sarybr=Enchantment Effect Colour: §7Pick the colour of the enchantment outline. Lots of colours to make your enchanted tools stand out.	#
text.oreville.qbscwk=Totem of Undying Opacity: §7Choose when your totem becomes see-through in first person. Makes the totem less distracting when you play while holding it in either hand. You can disable the effect if you want to always keep it fully opaque.	#
text.oreville.bbvkof=Enable Expressions: §7Give your player skin more life with blinking, eye movement, and animated eyebrows. If you experience issues with any of the skins you are using or on servers, you should disable this option.	#
text.oreville.qulasx=Customise how Actions & Stuff behaves to suit your playstyle. To configure Pack Settings, head to Actions & Stuff's Resource Pack and click the small Settings Icon.	#
text.oreville.amdosd=Pack Settings	#
text.oreville.fhkeks=§7§oNote: This is just the beginning for Pack Settings and we plan to continue updating this feature, let us know what you want to see next!	#
text.oreville.lycrmi=§7§oYou'll also notice the changelog has been moved from the Pack Settings screen to the new Actions & Stuff in-game Wiki page!	#
text.oreville.naxcad=A new pink panorama set in the Cherry Grove biome, with babies galore.	#
