text.oreville.xchtvf=Actions & Stuff has a few fun secrets and Easter eggs, how many can you find?	#
text.oreville.vwolta=Creeper Pig: §cPig §7- A reference to how the Creeper was accidentally created! Originally, the model was meant to be a pig, but a coding bug rotated the body upright.	#
text.oreville.vqazva=Enderman: §cBeanie§r, §cGreen §7- A reference to when Enderman originally featured green eyes in early Minecraft.	#
text.oreville.bmtkch=Glitched Villager: §cVillager32 §7- Callback to a bug in Actions & Stuff 1.0.	#
text.oreville.otkbzf=Pig: §cMuddy§r, §cMudster§r, §cMucky §7- A Muddy Pig has a rare chance of spawning naturally in the world, alternatively you can use the nametag to create one.	#
text.oreville.ertmwm=Slime: §cjeb_§r, §cRBG§r, §cDisco §7- Get the party started with an RGB slime, just like the Vanilla sheep!	#
text.oreville.ryoeuz=Warden: §cWilliam §7- Callback to "The Secrets of Minecraft" video on the Wardens creation.	#
text.oreville.zigcmu=Zombie: §cBrian §7- A spooky but familiar surprise awaits...	#
text.oreville.yothxo=Spoilers	#
text.oreville.jbinmh=§7The Oreville Logo appears in place of the Helmet Inventory UI slot. His name is Cole!	#
text.oreville.awjhma=§7Rana is the original Minecraft character.	#
text.oreville.vsyadi=§7The Charged Creeper gets even more electrified than normal.	#
text.oreville.hlzzkk=§7Wear a Turtle Helmet to see it come to life, and even swim with you!	#
text.oreville.lxxanb=§7Pumpkins come with face variations!	#
text.oreville.zfiffm=§7With a 3% chance of spawning, you may spot a pale pumpkin in your world!	#
text.oreville.xdjbuc=Allay: §cGoldie §7- A golden Allay can be found in the wild, or use the nametag to create one. A reference to Minecraft Legends!	#
text.oreville.wrippn=New sword swings, an adorable Bucket of Axolotl companion, animation-synced footsteps, and so much more! The little details that make a big difference.	#
