text.oreville.zjquqy=Pack Settings lets you customise how Actions & Stuff behaves to suit your playstyle. Adjust a range of options using sliders, toggles, and dropdowns to your liking.	#
text.oreville.hvivtu=Entity Biome Variants: §7Choose if special biome mob variants can spawn on their own, or only appear when you name a mob with a nametag.	#
text.oreville.lxpvey=Morphs: §7Replace your default player model with a range of fully custom 3D characters, each with different visuals, effects and unique animations.	#
text.oreville.yzcpnb=Axolotl Colour: §7Pick the colour of your axolotl in a bucket when you hold it in hand.	#
text.oreville.dgijxb=Armour Visibility: §7Choose how equipped armour shows up on you. See it on your arms in first person, keep the normal vanilla look, or hide it completely.	#
text.oreville.bidall=Tool Enchantment Glint: §7Choose how enchanted tools look in your hand. Add a custom outline, a custom glint, enable both, or turn both off and keep the vanilla style.	#
text.oreville.fxivmf=Enchantment Effect Colour: §7Pick the colour of the enchantment effect. Lots of colours to make your enchanted tools stand out.	#
text.oreville.loxkzb=Totem of Undying Opacity: §7Choose when your totem becomes see-through in first person. Makes the totem less distracting when you play while holding it in either hand. You can disable the effect if you want to always keep it fully opaque.	#
text.oreville.nydlul=Enable Expressions: §7Give your player skin more life with blinking, eye movement, and animated eyebrows. If you experience issues with any of the skins you are using, you should disable this option.	#
text.oreville.cbyaba=3D Tools: §7Replace the traditional 2D style tools in hand with fully custom 3D tool models.	#
text.oreville.oubwbt=Costumes: §7Turns some leather armour with trims into custom themed costumes. Only works with the Full Experience texture style.	#
text.oreville.kbikaw=How to configure Pack Settings:	#
text.oreville.krdfxm=Item Swap Sounds: §7Play a sound whenever you switch items in your hotbar.	#
text.oreville.njwgfc=Better Rain Particles: §7Choose between custom rain particles or the vanilla rain look.	#
text.oreville.fgtogl=Legacy Baby Chick Model: §7Switch between the Legacy Actions & Stuff Chick and new Tiny Takeover Chick model. You can also use the nametag "Peep" or "Hatchling" to have a mixture of both designs!	#
text.oreville.tvhaqo=1. Open Minecraft settings from the pause menu.	#
